Fahreza asked for a configure button next to the detach button and view configs like refresh rate; also challenged my earlier 'Enable agent control button' proposal — 'how do the other connectors/tools do it? See their pattern.'

THE PATTERN ANSWER: no connector has a separate enable step — ADDING the connector IS the enable (telegram: add with bot token -> enabled=1 -> agents reachable). So the gear panel's 'Agent control' line is deliberately a STATUS READOUT + link to /settings/connectors, not a second switch. The earlier button idea was off-pattern and dropped.

GEAR PANEL (AndroidLiveView.svelte): gear button grouped with detach/reattach (ml-auto moved from the individual buttons to a wrapper div; gear shows in rail AND detached window). Config strip: refresh rate select 400/1000/3000/10000ms — FRAME_GAP_MS const became frameGapMs state driving scheduleNextFrame, persisted as localStorage 'androidFrameGapMs' (read in onMount, SSR-safe; validated saved>0). The 10s battery-saver option addresses fahreza's laptop-heat complaint from the original rail work. Agent-control status fetched from /api/connectors on panel open (raw fetch — component stays self-contained, no $lib/api import, per its design).

CONNECTOR PICKER GATING (settings/connectors/+page.svelte): connectorTypes was a static list, so non-android builds showed the Android tile and creating one produced a dead record (create_connector's unknown-type fallback is a webhook — pre-existing wart, now load-bearing since the connector is the opt-in). Filtered via the same /v1/android/status application/json content-type probe as the layout rail (SPA fallback returns HTML). Also added hint copy to the android connector form: it grants agents the android_* tools and agents restart automatically.

KNOWN ROUGH EDGE: the 'Manage in Connectors' link inside the DETACHED window navigates that popup to the full app (chromeless route is only /android and /setup). Harmless but odd; fix would be opening the URL in the main window via Tauri event — not worth it yet.
